# How they're keeping (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): one asks after the other, who answers as they are today (hurt,
# grieving, hungry, flush, run off their feet, newly a parent), and the first answers that in kind (keeping.sorry,
# keeping.glad, keeping.nod), as they are: the warm offer soup, the cold shrug, the poor envy the rich. Or one tells
# the other, unasked, what's on their mind. Every beat is the speaker's own best rule, so one question has a hundred
# answers.
#
# Other files hand to keeping.sorry, keeping.glad and keeping.nod too, so their unkeyed rules must fit anything sad,
# glad or ordinary. The lines here remember what kind of thing was said (pair.mem.k: grief, want, hurt, robbed, scrap,
# good, family, jest, weary, old, hopes), and the replies keyed to it have priority 1, so a chain's best tier is always
# a reply to what was actually said ("If it's a matter of money" never answers a death).

## Asking after them

rule keep_ask
when concept=talk.day|talk.friends pair.band=acquaintances|friends|rivals|apprentice
cooldown 1d
say How are you keeping? | And how are you, #address#? | Keeping well? | All well with you? | How's the world treating you?
then other: keeping.answer

rule keep_ask_close
when concept=talk.day|talk.friends pair.band=friends|family|spouses self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 1d
say How are you keeping, #pet#? | Come on, then. How are you really? | Tell me how you are. Truly. | You've a look about you. All well?
then other: keeping.answer

rule keep_ask_chatty
when concept=talk.day|talk.friends|talk.smalltalk self.talk=chatty pair.band=acquaintances|friends|rivals
cooldown 1d
say Now, how are you? I've not seen you in an age. | Come here, tell me everything. How are you? | You first. How are things? | Well? Well? Don't keep me waiting. How are you?
then other: keeping.answer

rule keep_ask_formal
when concept=talk.day self.tone=formal pair.band!=family|spouses
cooldown 1d
say I trust you're keeping well? | And how do you fare? | I hope I find you well. | I hope the season has been kind to you.
then other: keeping.answer

rule keep_ask_gruff
when concept=talk.day self.tone=gruff pair.band!=strangers
cooldown 1d
say Still breathing, then? | You look terrible. How are you? | How's things. | Not dead yet?
then other: keeping.answer

## Answering, as they are (self is the one answering)

rule keep_well
when concept=keeping.answer
say Well enough. | Mustn't grumble. | Can't complain. Well, I can, but I won't. | Much the same as ever. | #saying#.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_mourning_kin
when concept=keeping.answer mourning=kin
priority 4
say ... Not well. Not well at all. | Their coat's still on the peg. I can't move it. | We buried one of ours. I'm still not right. | Don't. Please. I'll cry in the street.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 1m

rule keep_mourning_friend
when concept=keeping.answer mourning=friend
priority 3
say Lost a friend this week. It's sat on me. | Not so good. We lost someone. | You heard? About my friend? Aye. That. | Every joke I hear, I think: they'd have liked that.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 1m

rule keep_widowed
when concept=keeping.answer widowed=yes
say Quiet house, since. You get used to it. Mostly. | I talk to the walls now. They don't answer back, at least. | Getting by. It's the evenings. | I still cook for two. The neighbour's dog is very fat.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 1m

rule keep_hurt_bad
when concept=keeping.answer injured=bad
priority 3
say Not well. #hurt.capitalize# all over. | Can you not see? I can barely stand. | I've been better. Much better. #oath#. | Every breath's a knife. Don't make me laugh.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=hurt 1m

rule keep_hurt_light
when concept=keeping.answer injured=light
priority 1
say Bit #hurt#. Took a knock, nothing more. | Mending. Mind the paw. | Fine, but for the foreleg. It'll heal. | Bruised. My pride most of all.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=hurt 1m

rule keep_robbed
when concept=keeping.answer robbed=yes
priority 2
say Robbed! Took the lot. #robbery#. | Someone's been in my things. Took my #money#. | Furious. Robbed, in my own town. | I'd a purse this morning. I've a string now.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=robbed 1m

rule keep_fought
when concept=keeping.answer fought=yes
priority 1
say Sore. There was a fight. Don't ask. | Got into a scrap. You should see the other one. | Someone came at me. I gave as good as I got. | Still shaking, if I'm honest. There was a fight.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=scrap 1m

rule keep_homeless
when concept=keeping.answer homeless=yes
priority 3
say I've no roof, #address#. Sleeping where I can. | Out on my ear. Doorways, mostly. | Cold. Every night's cold without a door. | I sleep in the lee of the chapel. The stones keep the day's warmth a while.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_hungry
when concept=keeping.answer hungry=yes
priority 2
say #hungry.capitalize#, if I'm honest. | Haven't eaten since yesterday. | My belly's eating itself. | Light-headed. It's nothing a loaf wouldn't fix.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_destitute
when concept=keeping.answer wealth=destitute
priority 2
say Down to my last pennies. Lower. | Nothing left to sell but my coat. | Scraping, #address#. Scraping the pot. | I've pawned everything that'd pawn.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_poor
when concept=keeping.answer wealth=poor stage=adult|old
say Getting by. Just. | Every #money# counted twice. | Making it last, as ever. | Rent's paid. That's the best I can say.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_rich
when concept=keeping.answer wealth=rich
say Very well indeed. | Couldn't be better, thank you. | Oh, splendidly. A good year. | Very well. We've had the house done.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 1m

rule keep_dole
when concept=keeping.answer on_dole=yes
priority 1
say Living on the parish bread. It's bread. | On the dole. Don't look at me like that. | Queuing for loaves, like half the town. | The parish feeds me. I'm grateful. I hate it.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_owes
when concept=keeping.answer owes=yes
priority 1
say I owe more than I'm owed. Lie awake over it. | Debts, #address#. Debts on debts. | Ask me when I've paid what I owe. | There's a fellow I owe who's taken to waiting by my door.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_business_thriving
when concept=keeping.answer business=thriving
priority 1
say Run off my feet! Customers all day. | Never better. Can't keep the shelves full. | Busy, busy, busy. And glad of it. | Sold out before noon three days running.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 1m

rule keep_business_failing
when concept=keeping.answer business=failing
priority 2
say The shop's dying. Nobody's buying. | Not a coin in the till since Stoneday. | Another month like this and I'm shut. | I stand at the counter and listen to the street go by.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_tired
when concept=keeping.answer tired=yes
say #tired.capitalize#. #very.capitalize# #tired#. | Ready for #bed#, and it's not even dark. | Dead on my paws. | I could sleep on a fence.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=weary 1m

rule keep_at_work
when concept=keeping.answer working=yes shift=during
say Busy. I'm at it now, look. | Can't stop long. #work.capitalize#. | Well, but working. | Well, if they'd let me finish a thing.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_day_off
when concept=keeping.answer shift=day_off
say Day off! I mean to do nothing at all. | Grand. No #work# today. | A day to myself. Imagine. | Lovely. I slept till the sun was full up.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 1m

rule keep_spouse
when concept=keeping.answer self.spouse
cooldown 1d
say We're well, #self.spouse# and I. Thank you. | Well. #self.spouse# sends their best, I'm sure. | Can't complain. #self.spouse# does that for both of us. | Well. #self.spouse#'s cooking, so well fed.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 1m

rule keep_parent
when concept=keeping.answer self.child self.age<=36
cooldown 1d
say Busy. #self.child# keeps me on my toes. | Tired. #self.child# was up half the night. | #self.child#'s growing like a weed. I'm well. | Muddy. #self.child# found a puddle and brought it home.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 1m

rule keep_parent_grown
when concept=keeping.answer self.child self.age>=48
cooldown 1d
say Well. #self.child# came by on Restday. That makes a good week. | Proud. #self.child#'s doing well for themselves. | Well enough. #self.child# fusses over me now. Imagine. | Well. I've a grandpup on the way, they tell me.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 1m

rule keep_apprentice
when concept=keeping.answer apprentice=yes
say My master works me to the bone. But I'm learning. | Sore paws. Learning, though. | Still sweeping more than making. | I made a thing today that nobody threw away.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_master
when concept=keeping.answer master=yes
say Well, but for my apprentice. Ruined a day's work. | Teaching. It's harder than doing. | The young one's coming along. | My apprentice asks a question a breath. I've no breath left.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_old
when concept=keeping.answer stage=old
say Old, #address#. Old and creaking. But here. | Still above ground. | My hips know the weather before the sky does. | I've outlived my knees. The rest of me's holding.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=old 1m

rule keep_travelling
when concept=keeping.answer travelling=yes
say On the road again. Feet like boards. | Passing through. Always passing through. | Glad to sit a moment. | Three towns in four days. I've forgotten which this is.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_short
when concept=keeping.answer temper=short
say Why does everyone keep asking me that? | Fine. Is that all? | Same as yesterday. | Busy. Too busy for this.

rule keep_merry
when concept=keeping.answer humour=merry
cooldown 1d
say Better for seeing you! | Still handsome, still here. | Grand! Ask me again and I'll tell you a lie. | Never better. Well, once. I was nineteen.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=jest 1m

rule keep_devout
when concept=keeping.answer piety=devout
say Blessed, thank the Bright One. | Well, by the gods' grace. | Content. I've been to chapel. | Well. Every day's a gift, they say. Some are odd gifts.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_restless
when concept=keeping.answer drive=restless
cooldown 1d
say Same as ever. Same as ever. I need a change. | Bored, if I'm honest. Itching for something. | Wondering what's over the hill. | Restless. Like a dog before thunder.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=hopes 1m

rule keep_guarded
when concept=keeping.answer honesty=guarded
say Well enough. | Oh, you know. | Can't say I've anything to tell. | Same as anyone.
then other: keeping.nod

rule keep_sump
when concept=keeping.answer quarter=sump
cooldown 1d
say Water came up through the floor again. | Damp, #address#. It's the Sump. | Surviving. That's the Sump for you. | There's a crack in our wall you could post a letter through.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule keep_heights
when concept=keeping.answer quarter=heights
cooldown 1d
say Perfectly well. The Heights are dreadfully dull this season. | Very well, thank you. Such a bore at present. | Well. A great many dinners. | Well. I've been to three musical evenings this week. Three.
then other: keeping.nod

## Telling them, unasked

rule tell_rent
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day wealth=poor|destitute stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Rent's due and I've not got it. | Bread's gone up again and my purse hasn't. | I sold my good boots. Good boots! | I've let the fire go out to save the wood. In this.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule tell_flush
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Bought a new coat. Mossgrave wool. Feel that. | Had the roof done. Finally. | We're thinking of taking on another servant. | I've put by enough for three winters. I sleep like a pup.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 1m

rule tell_failing
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.work business=failing
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say Third day without a sale. | Nobody's buying. I've stock going stale. | I may have to let the shop go. | I've marked everything down. Still nobody.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule tell_thriving
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.work business=thriving
cooldown 2d
say Sold out by noon. Again. | I can't make it fast enough. | Best season I've had. | I had a queue out the door. A queue!
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 1m

rule tell_hurt
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day injured=bad
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say Look at this. Can't lift a thing. | Every step's a knife up the leg. | The healer says weeks. Weeks! | I slept sitting up. Lying down's worse.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=hurt 1m

rule tell_fought
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day fought=yes
cooldown 12h
say I was in a fight. I'm still shaking. | I've a lump on my head the size of an egg. | Somebody jumped me by the well. They'll think twice next time. | My ear's torn. Look. Somebody's teeth did that.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=scrap 1m

rule tell_robbed
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.crime robbed=yes
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say They robbed me. In my own town! | Someone took my things. Who does that? | #robbery#. I'm still shaking. | Cut my purse clean off my belt. I never felt a thing.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=robbed 1m

rule tell_hungry
when concept=talk.smalltalk hungry=yes
cooldown 2d
say My belly's been talking all morning. | I could eat a boot. Laces and all. | I keep walking past the bakery to smell it. | I've had a turnip since yesterday. Half a turnip.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule tell_mourning
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day|talk.friends mourning=kin
cooldown 12h
priority 2
say I can't stop thinking about them. | The house is so quiet. | I keep meaning to tell them things. | I found their boots by the door this morning. I can't move them.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 1m

rule tell_owes
when concept=talk.smalltalk owes=yes stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say I owe money to people I'd rather not. | If anyone asks, you've not seen me. | I borrowed to pay what I'd borrowed. It doesn't work. | Every knock at the door, I jump.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule tell_dole
when concept=talk.smalltalk on_dole=yes
cooldown 2d
say Queued two hours for the parish loaf. | The dole bread's stale again. | Never thought I'd take the parish's bread. | The parish clerk wrote my name in his book. Like a debt.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule tell_homeless
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day homeless=yes
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say Slept in a doorway again. | They put my things in the street. All of it. | The watch moved me on twice last night. | I had a door once. Blue. I miss the door.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 1m

rule tell_child
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.family|talk.friends self.child self.age<=36
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# asked me why the sky doesn't fall down. I'd no answer. | #self.child# lost a milk tooth! Kept it in a walnut shell. | #self.child# got into the flour bin. Came out white from ears to tail. | #self.child# has decided to be a horse. All day. Neighing.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 1m

rule tell_child_grown
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.family|talk.friends self.child self.age>=48
cooldown 3d
say #self.child# came for #supper#. Ate everything, left nothing, as ever. | #self.child#'s courting. At last. | #self.child# sent me a ham. A whole ham! | #self.child# asked my advice. Mine! I nearly fell over.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 1m

rule tell_spouse
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.family|talk.friends self.spouse
cooldown 2d
say #self.spouse# burnt the bread again. Don't tell anyone. | #self.spouse# snores like a mill. | #self.spouse# brought me flowers. No reason. I'm suspicious. | #self.spouse# has taken up the whistle. Badly.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 1m

rule tell_long_day
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.work tired=yes working=yes
cooldown 2d
say On my feet since dawn. | My back. My back! | One more hour. One more. | I've stopped feeling my paws. That's good, I think.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=weary 1m

rule tell_day_off
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.day shift=day_off
cooldown 2d
say Day off. I've no idea what to do with myself. | No #work# today. I could sing. | I slept till the sun was up. Bliss. | A whole day and nobody wanting anything of me.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 1m

rule tell_restless
when concept=talk.smalltalk drive=restless
cooldown 2d
say Some days I think I'll walk off down the road and not stop. | I'm sick of this town. Don't tell anyone. | One day I'll see the sea. Or the mountains. Somewhere. | Every cart that leaves, I watch it all the way out.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=hopes 1m

rule tell_ambitious
when concept=talk.smalltalk|talk.work drive=ambitious
cooldown 2d
say I'll have my own shop inside two years. Watch me. | I mean to be somebody. | There's money in this town if you're quick. | I've a plan. I'll not tell you it. But I've a plan.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=hopes 1m

## keeping.sorry (self is the one who asked, or listened). Unkeyed: fits any trouble, from any file.

rule sorry_plain
when concept=keeping.sorry
say I'm sorry to hear it. | That's hard. | #oath#. I'm sorry. | That's no good at all.

rule sorry_warm
when concept=keeping.sorry warmth=warm
say Come by mine tonight. There'll be soup. | Anything you need, you say it. | Oh, #pet#. Come here.

rule sorry_cold
when concept=keeping.sorry warmth=cold
say Mm. Well. | That's how it goes. | We all have our troubles.

rule sorry_close
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.band=friends|family|spouses
say You should have come to me sooner. | Why didn't you say? | I'm here. Whatever you need.

rule sorry_devout
when concept=keeping.sorry piety=devout
say I'll pray for you. I mean it. | The gods see it. They do. | I'll light a candle for you.

rule sorry_grief
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=grief
priority 1
say #oath#. I'm so sorry. | Take all the time it takes. | Is there anything I can do? Anything at all? | I'm sorry. I've no better words than that.

rule sorry_grief_warm
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=grief warmth=warm
priority 1
say Come here. Come here. | I'll bring something round tonight. You'll not have to cook. | Oh, #pet#. I'm so sorry.

rule sorry_grief_cold
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=grief warmth=cold
priority 1
say These things happen. I'm sorry. | It comes to all of us. | Well. You'll get through it. People do.

rule sorry_grief_old
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=grief stage=old
priority 1
say I've lost a few myself. It gets quieter. It's never gone. | At my age you know half the churchyard. It doesn't get easier. | Talk about them. That's what helps. Talk about them.

rule sorry_grief_devout
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=grief piety=devout
priority 1
say They're with the Bright One now. I'm sure of it. | I'll say their name at chapel. | The Bright One keeps them warm now.

rule sorry_grief_short
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=grief temper=short
priority 1
say Aye. Well. These things. | Hard luck. Truly. | I'm no good at this. I'm sorry.

rule sorry_want
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=want
priority 1
say Times are hard. For too many. | That's no way to live. It's not right. | Something'll turn. It has to. | That's a bad business.

rule sorry_want_helps
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=want self.wealth=rich|comfortable other.wealth=poor|destitute warmth=warm
priority 1
say If it's a matter of #money#, come and see me. | Let me help. No, I mean it. | Don't be proud. Not with me.

rule sorry_want_same
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=want wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Me too, #address#. Me too. | We're all in it. | You and half the town.

rule sorry_want_short
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=want temper=short
priority 1
say Well, don't stand there telling me, sort it. | And whose fault is that? | Everyone's got troubles.

rule sorry_want_dry
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=want humour=dry
priority 1
say Could be worse. Not much, mind. | Cheer up. Tomorrow could be worse still. | Well, at least you've your looks.

rule sorry_want_rich_cold
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=want self.wealth=rich warmth=cold
priority 1
say Have you thought of working harder? | I'm sure the parish will see you right. | One must cut one's coat, I suppose.

rule sorry_hurt
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=hurt
priority 1
say Let me see. Gods, that looks sore. | Sit down before you fall down. | You want that looked at. Properly. | Go easy. Let it mend.

rule sorry_hurt_warm
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=hurt warmth=warm
priority 1
say Lean on me. Where are you going? I'll walk you. | Let me carry that for you. | I've a salve at home. I'll fetch it round.

rule sorry_hurt_dry
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=hurt humour=dry
priority 1
say You'll do anything to get out of work. | Lost an argument with a staircase? | Well, it's improved your walk.

rule sorry_hurt_short
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=hurt temper=short
priority 1
say What did you do to yourself? | Then why are you out? Go home. | You'll make it worse, hobbling about.

rule sorry_robbed
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=robbed
priority 1
say Robbed! In broad day! It's not safe anywhere now. | Tell the watch. For all the good it'll do. | #oath#. I'll keep my purse closer. | That's wicked. Plain wicked.

rule sorry_robbed_short
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=robbed temper=short
priority 1
say I'd have their ears for it. | If I find them, they'll wish the watch had. | Hanging's too good.

rule sorry_robbed_poor
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=robbed wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say They'd get nothing off me. Nothing to get. | Robbing the likes of us. Have they no shame? | It's always us they rob. Never the Heights.

rule sorry_scrap
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=scrap
priority 1
say Keep your head down a while. | Somebody'll get hurt one of these days. Mind it's not you. | Fighting. It never ends well. | Let it lie, now. Let it lie.

rule sorry_scrap_warm
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=scrap warmth=warm
priority 1
say Let me see that eye. | Are you all right? Truly? Sit down. | Come home with me. I'll clean you up.

rule sorry_scrap_short
when concept=keeping.sorry pair.mem.k=scrap temper=short
priority 1
say Did you win, at least? | Next time, call me. | I'd have finished it for you.

## keeping.glad. Unkeyed: fits any good news or pleasant remark, from any file.

rule glad_plain
when concept=keeping.glad
say Ha! Good. | Well, there's a thing. | That's something, anyway. | Good. Good.

rule glad_warm
when concept=keeping.glad warmth=warm
say Oh, that's lovely to hear. | That does my heart good. | Isn't that grand!

rule glad_cold
when concept=keeping.glad warmth=cold
say Hm. | Fine. | Good.

rule glad_good
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=good
priority 1
say Good. Glad to hear it. | About time something went right. | Good for you. You've earned it. | Well, that's a fine thing.

rule glad_good_poor
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=good wealth=poor|destitute
priority 1
say Must be nice. | Some of us aren't so lucky. | Good for some.

rule glad_good_sly
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=good honesty=sly
priority 1
say Then you can buy the ale. | Lend us a penny, then. | Remember your friends, eh?

rule glad_good_ambitious
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=good drive=ambitious
priority 1
say Good. I'll catch you up, mind. | Lucky. I'll make my own luck. | Enjoy it. I'm coming for it.

rule glad_good_merry
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=good humour=merry
priority 1
say Then the ale's on you! | Ha! Let's have a song about it. | Grand! I'll tell everyone you're rich.

rule glad_good_devout
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=good piety=devout
priority 1
say The Bright One's been kind. Give thanks. | Blessings, all of them. Don't forget the chapel box. | That's the gods' favour, that is.

rule glad_family
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=family
priority 1
say Ha! That's family for you. | Give them my best. | Bless them. | They'll keep you young. Or old. One of the two.

rule glad_family_old
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=family stage=old
priority 1
say Make the most of it. It goes by quicker than you think. | Ah. I remember that. All of that. | Enjoy them. Even the noise.

rule glad_family_single
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=family !self.spouse
priority 1
say Sounds like a full house. Mine's a quiet one. | I'll take your word for it. | And here's me with nobody to burn my bread.

rule glad_family_dry
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=family humour=dry
priority 1
say And you'd not change a thing, I suppose. | Family life. They write songs about it. Sad ones. | That's love, that is. Apparently.

rule glad_family_warm
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=family warmth=warm
priority 1
say Oh, I love that. Tell them I said hello. | That's made my day, that has. | Bring them by. I've honey cakes.

rule glad_jest
when concept=keeping.glad pair.mem.k=jest
priority 1
say Ha! You never change. | Get away with you. | You're a tonic, you are. | Ha! Some things stay the same, thank the gods.

## keeping.nod. Unkeyed: fits any ordinary remark, from any file.

rule nod_plain
when concept=keeping.nod
say Aye. | Is that so. | Mm. Well. | #agree#.

rule nod_merry
when concept=keeping.nod humour=merry
say Ha! That's the way of it. | Ha! Isn't it always. | Well, there's life for you.

rule nod_tired
when concept=keeping.nod tired=yes
say Mm. I'm too #tired# to say more than aye. | I could sleep where I stand, myself. | Aye. Is it #bed# yet?

rule nod_old
when concept=keeping.nod stage=old other.stage!=old
say Ah. I remember. | Ha. Same as it ever was. | You're young yet.

rule nod_chatty
when concept=keeping.nod self.talk=chatty
say Oh, I know just what you mean. My cousin was the same. | Isn't that just the way? Same with me, near enough. | Don't I know it! Now, let me tell you...

rule nod_quiet
when concept=keeping.nod self.talk=quiet
say Mm. | Aye. | ...

rule nod_weary
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=weary
priority 1
say You and me both. | Get off your feet, then. | Sit a minute. The work'll wait. | Go home and sleep. That's an order.

rule nod_weary_tired
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=weary tired=yes
priority 1
say Don't talk to me about it. | Aye. #tired.capitalize#, the lot of us. | If you find a bed, tell me where.

rule nod_weary_old
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=weary stage=old other.stage!=old
priority 1
say Wait till you're my age. | Tired? You've no idea, pup. | At your age I worked two days in one. Or so I tell everyone.

rule nod_old_answer
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=old
priority 1
say You look well on it. | Still the sharpest one in the street. | Here's to many more creaks. | You'll see us all out.

rule nod_old_answer_old
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=old stage=old
priority 1
say Aye. Me too. We'll creak together. | Don't talk to me about knees. | We're the last of the old lot, you and me.

rule nod_old_answer_young
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=old stage=young
priority 1
say Are you very old? Older than the chapel? | My #gran# creaks too. | Can I hear you creak?

rule nod_hopes
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=hopes
priority 1
say Big talk. Good luck to you. | Mind you don't forget us when you do. | Ha! Well, someone should. | I'll believe it when I see it.

rule nod_hopes_content
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=hopes drive=content
priority 1
say Not me. I like it here. | Grass is greener, they say. It isn't. | What's wrong with here?

rule nod_hopes_restless
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=hopes drive=restless|ambitious
priority 1
say Take me with you. | I've thought the same. More than once. | Let me know when. I mean it.

rule nod_hopes_old
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=hopes stage=old other.stage!=old
priority 1
say I said that at your age. Here I still am. | Go while your legs are good. | Dream it while you can.

rule nod_hopes_short
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=hopes temper=short
priority 1
say Talk's cheap. | Then stop talking and do it. | You've said that before.

rule nod_hopes_warm
when concept=keeping.nod pair.mem.k=hopes warmth=warm
priority 1
say You will, too. I can see it in you. | Go on, then. I'll cheer you off. | You deserve it. Whatever it is.
